{"id":"a7","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":11,"of":16,"title":"In, to, from","titleHe":"מִלּוֹת יַחַס","goal":"Attach בְּ, לְ and מִ, and combine them with the article.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Three of the commonest prepositions are single letters glued to the front of the word: בְּ in or at, לְ to, מִ from."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"בְּבַיִת","en":"in a house"},{"he":"לְעִיר","en":"to a city"},{"he":"מִסֵּפֶר","en":"from a book"}]},{"type":"text","body":"When the word is definite, the הַ doesn't survive alongside them — it merges into the preposition's vowel."},{"type":"table","caption":"With the article","head":["indefinite","definite"],"rows":[["בְּבַיִת — in a house","בַּבַּיִת — in the house"],["לְעִיר — to a city","לָעִיר — to the city"],["מִבַּיִת — from a house","מֵהַבַּיִת — from the house"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"מִ is the exception: it keeps the הַ visible and lengthens its own vowel instead — מֵהַבַּיִת, not מַבַּיִת."}],"vocab":[{"he":"בְּ","en":"in, at","translit":"be-"},{"he":"לְ","en":"to, for","translit":"le-"},{"he":"מִ","en":"from","translit":"mi-"},{"he":"עִם","en":"with","translit":"im"},{"he":"אֶל","en":"to, towards","translit":"el"},{"he":"בֵּין","en":"between","translit":"bein"},{"he":"לְיַד","en":"next to","translit":"leyad"},{"he":"תַּחַת","en":"under","translit":"tachat"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["onion","struggle","in, at","right, privilege"],"correct":2,"prompt":"בְּ","translit":"be-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bear","ceiling","to, for","him, it"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לְ","translit":"le-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["light","cheese","sees","from"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מִ","translit":"mi-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["between","building","but rather","with"],"correct":3,"prompt":"עִם","translit":"im"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["at all, in general","youth, boy","death","to, towards"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אֶל","translit":"el"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["eats","pain","plays","between"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בֵּין","translit":"bein"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["next to","my, mine","son","bedroom"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לְיַד","translit":"leyad"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["בְּ","in, at"],["לְ","to, for"],["מִ","from"],["עִם","with"],["אֶל","to, towards"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “in, at”?","options":["מְשַׁעֲמֵם","שֶׁלּוֹ","לֹא","בְּ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “next to”?","options":["צָרָה","לְיַד","כִּכָּר","אֵינֶנִּי"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “between”?","options":["מְקַבֵּל","שָׂם","בֵּין","חוֹשֵׁב"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “under”?","options":["מְעַט","בִּכְלָל","תַּחַת","כָּךְ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["לְ","עִם","תַּחַת","בְּ"],"correct":3,"say":"בְּ","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"“In the city” is —","options":["בָּעִיר","בְּהָעִיר","בַּעִיר","בְּעִיר"],"correct":0,"why":"The article merges into the preposition; because עִיר starts with ע the vowel is kamatz, giving בָּעִיר. בְּעִיר without it means in a city."},{"type":"read","he":"לְ","translit":"le-","en":"to, for"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “to, for” in Hebrew","answer":"לְ","hint":"le-"}]}